# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secret-adjacent local artefacts.
#
# These files were sitting untracked AND un-ignored in the repository root.
# Nothing is deleted by this change: the files stay on disk exactly as they
# are, they are simply never staged and never uploaded.
#
# `admin.txt` and `bank details.txt` are local working documents that may hold
# credentials. `r2-object-keys.json` is a Cloudflare R2 object listing, which is
# infrastructure reconnaissance rather than source. The remaining entries are
# captured HTTP responses and build/scratch output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/admin.txt
/body.txt
/cart.txt
/details.txt
/r2-object-keys.json
/r2-object-keys-*.json
/r2-missing.txt
/r2-upload-completed.txt
/r2-test-banner.*
/build.log
/output/
/working/
/catalogue-view-qa-output.txt
/dashboard-text-*.txt
/smoke-test-results.*
/preview-*.txt

# Private keys and credential material, regardless of extension.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.netrc

# `.env.r2.example` is a documentation template and SHOULD be committed, but
# `.env.*` above swallows it. The narrow un-ignore below fixes that without
# widening the exception to every future example file.
!.env.r2.example
!.env.*.example
